<figure
  class="inventory-lifecycle"
  aria-labelledby="inventory-lifecycle-caption"
  aria-describedby="inventory-lifecycle-text"
>
  <p id="inventory-lifecycle-text" class="lifecycle-text">
    Generic source domains move through matching and normalization, movement and coverage
    measures, three separate scenario models, validation gates, an explainable
    recommendation, and final business review.
  </p>
  <p class="sequence-cue">Follow stages 01–07.</p>
  <ol class="lifecycle-steps">
    <li>
      <span class="stage-type">Inputs</span>
      <strong>Source domains</strong>
      <small>
        Bring the required product, inventory, sales, and economic context together.
      </small>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="stage-type">Preparation</span>
      <strong>Matching and normalization</strong>
      <small>
        Connect records and make classifications and measurement inputs comparable.
      </small>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="stage-type">Movement</span>
      <strong>Velocity and inventory coverage</strong>
      <small>Relate recent movement to the aged quantity under review.</small>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="stage-type">Scenarios</span>
      <strong>Three financial paths</strong>
      <small>
        Model removal or disposal, discounted sell-through, and liquidation separately.
      </small>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="stage-type">Controls</span>
      <strong>Validation gates</strong>
      <small>
        Hold incomplete or unsuitable records for review instead of forcing an answer.
      </small>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="stage-type">Output</span>
      <strong>Explainable recommendation</strong>
      <small>
        Present the strongest or least-negative modeled result with a plain-English
        reason.
      </small>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="stage-type">Authority</span>
      <strong>Business review</strong>
      <small>
        Apply operational eligibility and additional context before choosing the action.
      </small>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <figcaption id="inventory-lifecycle-caption" class="caption">
    A data-free lifecycle illustrating how a financial comparison can remain traceable
    from source preparation through human review. Numbering, headings, and descriptions
    communicate the sequence without relying on color.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

